       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3200 mg/day under physician supervision, and 1200 mg/day is the usual over-the-counter limit.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory regimen.\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day), the maximum daily dose.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, a typical analgesic regimen.\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the order note."
