     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose this high. At 6400 mg/day, the patient would get twice the maximum daily dose and double the maximum single dose. That carries a real risk of serious harm, such as GI bleeding or acute kidney injury, and no monitoring plan I know of makes it safe. Ibuprofen also has a ceiling effect, so higher doses add toxicity without adding pain relief.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, three times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (2400 mg/day).\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain or inflammation control, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. For example, scheduled acetaminophen (up to 1000 mg every 8 hours, or 3 g/day) alongside ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n\nIf there's a specific protocol or indication behind the 1600 mg dose, you can place the order directly in the order-entry system. That would go through pharmacy review, which would also check it.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
